{"symbol":"TKA.DE","area":"europe","updated":"2026-11-09T20:25:38Z","info":{"address1":"thyssenkrupp Allee 1","address2":"Postfach P.O. Box, 45063","city":"Essen","zip":"45143","country":"Germany","phone":"49 201 844 0","fax":"49 201 844 536000","website":"https://www.thyssenkrupp.com","industry":"Conglomerates","industryKey":"conglomerates","industryDisp":"Conglomerates","sector":"Industrials","sectorKey":"industrials","sectorDisp":"Industrials","longBusinessSummary":"thyssenkrupp AG, together with its subsidiaries, provides industrial and technology solutions and services in Germany and internationally. The company operates in five segments: Automotive Technology, Decarbon Technologies, Materials Services, Steel Europe, and Marine Systems. It offers axle assembly and logistics, body in white, camshafts and electric engine components, carValoo, dampers, dies, plant engineering for batteries and powertrain, prototypes, serial production, springs and stabilizers, steering, crankshafts and conrods, thermal management, and undercarriages, as well as systems, automation, and mechatronic solutions; and slewing bearings and rings, chemical plants, coke plant technologies, green ammonia, methanol, and hydrogen, high-pressure processing, refinery services and cement plants. The company also provides alloys, logistics services, industrial minerals, material services, nonferrous metals, plastics, and stainless steel; composite materials, cut-to-length sheet products, electrical and packaging steel, hot and precision steel strips, organic coated strips and sheets, and sheet and coated products; and naval services, surface vessels, and submarines. It serves automotive, chemicals, energy generation and distribution, food and beverages, white goods, aerospace, mechanical and plant engineering, oil and gas, shipbuilding, and special vehicles, as well as construction, infrastructure, and buildings industries. In addition, The company operates as global materials distributor and technical and infrastructural service provider The company was founded in 1811 and is headquartered in Essen, Germany.","fullTimeEmployees":89813,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Miguel Angel Lopez Borrego","age":60,"title":"CEO & Chairman of the Executive Board","yearBorn":1965,"fiscalYear":2024,"totalPay":2344000,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Dr. Volkmar  Dinstuhl","age":53,"title":"CEO of Multi Tracks and Automotive Technology segment & Member of Executive Board","yearBorn":1972,"fiscalYear":2024,"totalPay":1115825,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Ilse Irene Henne","age":53,"title":"Member of Executive Board","yearBorn":1972,"fiscalYear":2024,"totalPay":1096825,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Dr. Axel  Hamann","age":51,"title":"CFO & Member of Executive Board","yearBorn":1974,"fiscalYear":2024,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Wilfried  von Rath","age":61,"title":"Chief Human Resources Officer & Member of Executive Board","yearBorn":1964,"fiscalYear":2024,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Thomas S. Empelmann","title":"Head of Corporate Finance","fiscalYear":2024,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Andreas  Trösch","age":58,"title":"Head of Investor Relations","yearBorn":1967,"fiscalYear":2024,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Dr. Stefan  Schmitt","age":49,"title":"Head of Corp. Function HR Strategy and Head of Corp. Function People Dev & Executives Management","yearBorn":1976,"fiscalYear":2024,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Peter  Walker","age":62,"title":"Chief Executive Officer of Elevator Technology Business Area","yearBorn":1963,"fiscalYear":2024,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Volker  Hellberg","title":"Chief Executive Officer of Industrial Solutions Unit - Saudi Arabia","fiscalY